GitHub is a web-based platform for version control and collaboration, built on Git, that helps developers store, manage, and share their code, track project progress, and work together on software projects with features like issue tracking, pull requests, and code reviews, making it a central hub for developers worldwide. It provides a graphical interface and hosting for Git repositories, enabling remote teamwork, while Git handles local version management




